id: pm-github-xhtp
title: Explain privacy matches and distinguish bare-root regex literals during gated sync
description: "Fix GitHub issue #160: the public pm-web issue 218 regex literal is classified as an absolute host root. Preserve path refusals in every imported field, provide safe match evidence, and verify no-git refusal."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#160"
created_at: "2026-10-21T04:40:30.603Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:51:53.756Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T18:51:50.084Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:51:50.084Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The public pm-web issue 218 text and comments import through ordinary and atomic gated modes.; Actual host paths in titles, bodies, comments and labels are refused before tracker mutation.; Refusals identify the item and published field with a safe excerpt and character offset.; A real plain tracker outside Git receives a clear refusal with no imported item writes.; Behavioral reverts fail the targeted regressions and npm and Bun release gates retain all original thresholds."
resolution: "Reverified main eebda9277e52 (unchanged since audit): [PR #162](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/162) (eebda92) distinguishes bare-root regex literals and returns redacted privacy-match diagnostics. Retained evidence: gate.ts, test/coverage-edges.test.ts, test/gate-inputs.test.ts."
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T04:41:06.116Z",codex-agent,"Read issue #160 and fetched pm-web issue 218 plus both public comments using read-only GitHub REST calls. The body regex literal produces one absolute-host-path match at body offset 2229; SHA-256 71708eb255bc230cd7c91dd26f7667a7b9386a2dc1f09756555c2c5c8bdc3c47 exactly matches the failed workflow receipt. The match is a bare root token inside JavaScript regex source, not an importer-added path or a GitHub URL. Plan: narrowly distinguish that regex syntax, add redacted match evidence to both report formats, and test real temporary tracker imports plus missing-repository refusal."
  "2026-10-21T04:44:12.762Z",codex-agent,"Implemented a narrow exception for bare root tokens followed by JavaScript regex source and test/exec invocation. Slash-separated paths remain scanned, including inside regex source. Reports now carry match_offset and a redacted excerpt; host paths reveal only the root initial and other findings use a fixed redaction marker. Read-only public fixture imports pass in ordinary and atomic modes; adversarial title/body/comment/label paths fail before any tracker mutation. Strengthened the existing no-git test to initialize a real plain tracker with a Git discovery ceiling."
  "2026-10-21T04:44:57.092Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restoring only HOST_PATH_RULES makes both the real public issue import regression and the bare-root regex regression fail (2/2 failures), retaining the exact reported hash. Restoring only scanChangeFile, runTrackerGate and formatGateReport makes both the redacted evidence regression and the adversarial imported-field diagnostics regression fail (2/2 failures). Restored the fix after each experiment. Baseline before edits also failed both new import tests. No history was rewritten."
  "2026-10-21T04:47:01.359Z",codex-agent,"Review tightened regex recognition to require an expression boundary and forbid crossing quotes, escapes, newlines or additional slashes. Added quoted-path and shell-text adversarial cases. Linked tests ran through pm test --run --progress: 2/2 commands passed (3 import/no-git tests and 12 scanner/input tests). The tracker has test-result tracking disabled, so results are recorded here rather than changing project policy. Final scanner-only revert now restores scanLineForRuleHits; evidence-function revert remains independently verified."
  "2026-10-21T04:51:40.978Z",codex-agent,"The first clean-HOME release gate passed typecheck/build/docstrings/lint/duplication/privacy (6121 objects), then test compilation found two missing test type updates. Updated the manually constructed GateFinding fixture with match evidence and narrowed the import result before asserting imported count. Thresholds and runtime behavior are unchanged. Final scanLineForRuleHits-only behavioral revert independently failed both relevant regressions (2/2), and the fixed scanner was restored."
  "2026-10-21T05:15:04.991Z",codex-agent,"Stopped an intermediate full coverage run after 126 reported passes and no reported failures to harden the new helper against long malformed whitespace. The regex now consumes exactly one leading whitespace character before its remaining source class, avoiding overlapping whitespace quantifiers. Added a 100000-space malformed-source case and a multiple-space valid-regex case. Restarting the complete clean-environment release gate on the final scanner; no thresholds, pins or source exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-21T07:11:56.552Z",codex-agent,"Complete clean-environment npm run release:check passed: 983/983 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips. Exact coverage across all 16 authored modules: lines and statements 11086/11086, functions 303/303, branches 3539/3539. Duplication zero, production audit zero vulnerabilities, privacy audit passed, package dry-run and canonical changelog check passed, release publish attestation passed. The real public issue import, adversarial field refusals, native Bun repeat acceptance and no-git refusal all passed in the full run. Isolated-global strict health and validation passed, with zero history drift. Starting the Bun release gate on unchanged executable source and tests."
  "2026-10-21T08:27:35.749Z",codex-agent,"Complete clean-environment bun run release:check passed: 983/983 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips. All 16 authored modules again measured exact coverage: lines and statements 11086/11086, functions 303/303, branches 3539/3539. Every remaining release gate passed at original thresholds, including privacy, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, packaging, changelog and publish attestation. Final pm test --run --progress rerun passed both linked commands (3 import/no-git tests plus 12 scanner/input tests). Test-result persistence remains disabled by existing policy, so results are preserved in comments. Final isolated-global strict health and validation passed with zero history drift; only existing advisory tracker warnings remain. Ready for PR review. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or package release."
  "2026-10-21T08:49:00.843Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #162: fetched all review threads with every comment (2 unresolved, no pagination) and latest CodeRabbit review (no Outside diff range findings). Both findings verified against gate.ts: quoted paths can satisfy the regex exception; entropy offsets point at the assignment rather than its matched value. Self-review also found the same offset mismatch for home-username matches with consumed delimiters. Plan: quote-aware regex recognition preserving whole serialized fields, exact captured-value offsets, behavioral revert proofs and unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Branch is current with remote and already contains main."
  "2026-10-21T08:54:24.050Z",codex-agent,"Implemented both valid review findings: PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6usDDD now rejects regex-shaped bare roots inside single, double and template string quotes, respecting escaped quotes and valid whole JSON/TOON string serialization. PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM6usDDe now uses capture-group indices for the hashed entropy value. Whole-PR self-review found and fixed the same consumed-prefix offset defect in home-username matches. Regressions cover raw/serialized strings, escaped quotes/backslashes, multiline templates, Markdown fences, Unicode escape offsets, repeated assignments and explicit history diffs in a real non-git tracker. Original ordinary and atomic public fixture imports still pass (3/3 targeted import tests). Targeted scanner/input tests pass 17/17; every new source branch is covered in the targeted c8 receipt. Build, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gate passed."
  "2026-10-21T08:54:25.565Z",codex-agent,"Review-round behavioral revert proofs: restored only isBareRootRegex from the pre-review HEAD, retaining all regression tests; node --test --test-name-pattern \"quoted host roots\" test/gate-inputs.test.ts failed 1/1 (missing finding). Restored only scanLineForRuleHits from that HEAD; node --test --test-name-pattern \"secret offsets|home-username offsets\" test/gate-inputs.test.ts failed 2/2 (secret offset 0 rather than 9; home offset 3 rather than 4). Each changed function was restored immediately afterward. Fixed-code rerun of those three regressions plus the real non-git history/report regression passed 4/4. Tests import source directly, so rebuilds do not mask these proofs."
  "2026-10-21T08:58:20.968Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review found that normalizing three backslashes before an escaped quote can change quote parity in raw source. Preserve both original and normalized quote states; valid serialized fields use their decoded source state. Extended the quoted-path regression accordingly. Stopped the first npm gate deliberately to make this correction; its incomplete coverage output is not an acceptance result. Repeated final-code function-only revert proofs: old isBareRootRegex fails 1/1 quoted-path tests; old scanLineForRuleHits fails 2/2 offset tests. Independently removing only original-source quote-state preservation fails the quoted-path test on the three-backslash case (1/1). Fixed-code targeted tests pass 5/5; source/test compilation and lint pass. Restart both full release gates on the final source."
  "2026-10-21T09:03:51.166Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after a transient provider interruption: git status confirms only the intended code, documentation, tests and tracker evidence are changed. The claimed item and all revert proofs are intact. Final targeted Node and native Bun scanner tests passed 17/17 and both linked pm test commands passed. The provider interruption terminated the restarted npm release gate before any summary or exit receipt; this is an incomplete run, not a test failure. Restarting only the incomplete full release gates in a detached process with durable exit receipts."
  "2026-10-21T09:34:47.433Z",codex-agent,"Completed the remaining quote-context self-review. Raw field text beginning with a TOON-like label must not receive tracker serialization privileges; scanChangeFile now explicitly identifies serialized TOON lines and planned/history field values remain decoded data. Earlier regexes containing quotes or character classes must not cancel a later real string: the linear quote scan keeps both slash interpretations conservatively and recognizes complete Markdown fences. The original public issue still imports in ordinary and atomic modes (3/3 import regressions), and scanner/input tests pass 18/18. Targeted c8 verifies every new helper/scanner branch is exercised. Build, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. Stopped the incomplete npm run to apply these valid same-class corrections; no full-gate acceptance is claimed for that run."
  "2026-10-21T09:34:49.155Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round behavioral revert receipt on restored final source: isBareRootRegex-only revert fails 1/1 quoted-path regressions; scanLineForRuleHits-only revert fails 2/2 entropy/home-offset regressions. Independently reverting original quote-state preservation, tracker serialization context, and slash interpretation handling each fails 1/1 corresponding regressions. Total: 6 expected assertion failures across 5 independent experiments, each with exit 1; fixes restored after every experiment. Tests import source directly. Logs contain only synthetic fixtures; no history was rewritten."
  "2026-10-21T10:31:04.997Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated npm run release:check passed with exit 0: 989/989 tests, zero failures, cancellations or skips. Exact coverage for all 16 authored modules: lines and statements 11169/11169, functions 305/305, branches 3603/3603. Original four 100 percent thresholds and source inventory are unchanged. Every remaining release check passed, including typecheck/build/docstrings/lint, zero duplication, privacy audit, zero production vulnerabilities, package dry-run, canonical changelog and publish attestation. Source/test hashes are identical before and after the run; its coverage receipt was preserved separately. Both linked pm test commands also passed (3 import tests plus 18 scanner/input tests), and native Bun passed all 18 scanner/input tests. Existing test-result tracking is disabled, so receipts remain in comments. The full isolated Bun release gate is now running on unchanged source."
  "2026-10-21T10:34:07.880Z",codex-agent,"Upstream main advanced during the full gates with the daily package version update (PR #163), making this PR one commit behind. Merged origin/main into the working branch as required; the upstream delta changes only package/version metadata, the index.ts version constant and the changelog date. Review fixes, tests and behavioral revert proofs are unchanged. Preserved the completed npm 989/989 and 100/100/100/100 receipt for the pre-merge source. Stopped the incomplete Bun run, and will run both full release gates against the merged package version rather than treating the older metadata receipt as final acceptance."
  "2026-10-21T10:35:43.298Z",codex-agent,Post-merge build and isolated pm strict health passed with zero history drift and no pending merge receipts. No reconciliation or history rewrite was necessary. The review fix and regression files are unchanged by the upstream merge. Starting both complete release gates on package version 2026.10.21; each run will preserve its own coverage summary and source hashes.
  "2026-10-21T11:12:57.283Z",codex-agent,"Complete isolated npm run release:check passed on the merged 2026.10.21 package with exit 0: 989/989 tests; zero failures, cancellations or skips. All 16 authored modules retain exact coverage: lines/statements 11169/11169, functions 305/305, branches 3603/3603. All source/test/config JSON and executable source hashes match before and after the run. Every release check passed at unchanged thresholds, including privacy, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, packaging, canonical changelog and publish attestation. The merged-head coverage receipt is separate from the earlier pre-main receipt. The complete isolated Bun release gate is now running on the same frozen source."
  "2026-10-21T11:45:04.247Z",codex-agent,"Both complete isolated release gates now pass on the merged 2026.10.21 source: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each exit 0, each with 989/989 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Each independently measured all 16 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100: lines/statements 11169/11169, functions 305/305, branches 3603/3603. All executable source, test and tracked JSON hashes match before/after each gate and match the final working source. Privacy, zero duplication, zero production vulnerabilities, package dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation gates pass at original thresholds. Five behavioral revert experiments produced six expected assertion failures, with all fixes restored; both original unresolved review findings and the same-class self-review cases are covered. Linked pm tests passed 2/2 commands (21 tests) and native Bun scanner tests passed 18/18. No Outside diff range findings were present in the fetched CodeRabbit review. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; releasing the claim before committing code and append-only pm evidence. Review threads will remain untouched."
